<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/dopamine.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1058944" />After 326 days, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-26/">iOS 26</a> has received its first jailbreak, thanks to the developers behind the popular Dopamine jailbreak.<br/>
<br/>
Lars Fröder, better known as opa334, today released <a href="https://ellekit.space/dopamine/">Dopamine 3.0</a>, which adds support for a number of newer firmware versions, including iOS 26.0 and iOS 26.0.1 on devices with A12 or A13 chips.<br/>
<br/>
Another major addition in today's release is support for all devices running iOS 16.5.1 through iOS 17.3.1, significantly expanding the range of devices and software versions compatible with Dopamine.<br/>
<br/>
